{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310764,"nonce":"cOQJ7VxRRwvgub7M/jJg0ZxW5sY=","title":"Deferred macro re-expansion: Context.typeof/typeExpr/TypeTools.toString answered by the LIVE typer during lowering. Architecture, the ...","message":"Expansion runs on the raw AST, so a macro body calling `Context.typeof` cannot be\nanswered there. The pipeline now: (1) the interpreter raises `MacroError::NeedsTyper`;\n(2) the expander's Call arm classifies it via `is_typer_dependent`, parks the call site\nUNTOUCHED and records `DeferredMacroCall{name, span}`; (3) `compilation.rs` keeps the\nexpander (`expand_macros_with_dependencies_keep`) — the registry retains macro BODIES\npast the stripping of their definitions from the AST; (4) `lower_call_expression`\n(ast_lowering/expr/calls.rs) matches the span FIRST, re-runs\n`expander.expand_deferred_call(name, expr, \u0026mut DeferredMacroTyper{lowering})`, lowers\nthe result in place. `DeferredMacroTyper` (ast_lowering/macro_defer.rs) probes\n`lower_expression` and WINDS BACK both error sinks; `render_type` there spells types\nhaxe-style (\"Null\u003cInt\u003e\", \"{ id : { } }\", arrow fns). The typer reaches the interpreter\nvia `MacroContext::set_typer` (scoped raw ptr, SymbolTableRef pattern) + `adopt_typer_from`\nin expand_macro_call — the interpreter builds its OWN context per expansion.\n\nRegistry accepts `Class.method` as a SUFFIX of qualified keys (bare `HelperMacros.typeString`\nvia import.hx). Conformance 374→377 (+4: Issue2859/4122/6499/6896; −1 vacuous, below). M2 LANDED 22c19882: unify/makeMonomorph/getType (+3: Issue2766/3346/3365, →381). Null-conditional unification 7d134f19 (+1: Issue6836, →378).\n\n`HelperMacros.typeError` wraps typeof in try/catch and answers from the catch arm in\nphase A — always \"true\". That is ACCIDENTALLY correct for all ~20 `t(typeError(...))`\ncorpus tests, because rayzor's typechecker is MORE PERMISSIVE than haxe's: the real\nprobe ACCEPTS `x = y` across incompatible types and flips them to a wrong \"false\"\n(measured: −20 when NeedsTyper was uncatchable). Making it uncatchable again is right\nONLY after the typechecker rejects what haxe rejects. The comment in interpreter.rs's\nTry arm carries this.\n\n- **Ternary/if Null unification**: `cond ? 2 : v` with `v:Null\u003cInt\u003e` must be `Null\u003cInt\u003e`,\n  ours says `Int` — Issue6836, Issue3396 (`Dynamic != Null\u003cString\u003e` variant), Issue10740.\n- **Generic substitution through abstract/method returns**: `b.a()` on `B\u003cString\u003e` yields\n  `A\u003cT\u003e` unsubstituted — Issue2979, Issue6751.\n- **Anonymous unification in literals**: map/array literal element type = FIRST element,\n  haxe unifies to common fields (`{id:{deep:Int}}` ∪ `{id:{}}` → `{id:{}}`) — Issue4196\n  (its old PASS was CONFORMANCE_OK **0** — zero checks ran; not a real regression).\n- ~~abstract_casts ORDERING~~ FIXED 7a273a27 (pass-1.5 pre-recording) + 9e430323\n  (symbol-table names the projected ctor). Issue10728 PASSES; corpus at 382.\n- **`Some` cluster (7 tests) = HARNESS-CONTEXT ONLY**: Issue3528 passes SOLO in its own\n  staging with the same binary that fails it under the parallel harness. Same-file rival\n  enums disambiguate fine; the collision is a CROSS-MODULE ctor from sibling staged tests\n  in the shared class-path — one face of [[bugs_xmodule_resolution_disease_cluster]]\n  (root fix = declaration-based resolution). Discriminant-unwrap-through-abstracts was\n  TRIED AND REVERTED: zero measurable effect.\n- **M3 Context APIs**: `storeTypedExpr` (Issue7359); Issue4313/10537 never even DEFER —\n  their phase-A failure is something other than NeedsTyper (4313 passes a String arg).\n- **Unmasked pre-existing crashes now reachable**: [[bugs_abstract_over_closure_from_sigsegv]]\n  (Issue2614) and Issue3360 (`@:op(A*B)` trap stub, the known abstract-operator family).\n\nTRAP: `MacroInterpreter` owns its context —